asciianm  Ascii Animation program 

v.1 PRE RELEASE (1998)

v.2 28/8/2002
asciianm.c :
             - Dior8osi  Warnings
             - Metafora tou field descriptor stis ka8olikes diloseis
             - klisimo tou field descriptor kai ston termination_handler.
             - Metafora tou orismatos speed proto meta to onoma tou arxeiou
             - Pros8iki tis litourgias info
             - Pros8iki tis parametrou comment (emfanizete apo to info)
             - alagi me8odou emfanisis sti o8oni, katargisi ton display,
               flagtimer kai pros8iki ton timer_handler, display_kare, 
               display_file kai ton metavliton play, karef kai pid
	     - Pros8iki dinatotitas xirismou o8onis me ansi
             - Pros8iki dinatotitas compile xoris ncurses (mono ansi)			 
	     - Pros8iki parametrou -v  --version (version)

25/11/2026 (for the vt100-animations repository)
timer.c :
             - A speed of 1000 ms or more did not start the timer at all
             - cleartimer stops the timer
asciianm.c :
             - SIGALRM only inside sigsuspend, the file is closed after every
               repetition (many repetitions could crash the program)
             - int ch in place of char ch (no end of file where char is unsigned,
               e.g. Linux on ARM)
             - The author's old e-mail address was removed
             - The last frame of every pass is seen as long as the others (it was
               seen twice as long, because the end of the file took one more tick)
             - Keys: q quit, space pause, + and - speed
             - The last frame stays on the screen at the end, with ncurses too; with
               -ansi the cursor goes below it (when the output is a file: line 17, as before)
             - The messages are in English. A change of the size of the window does
               not start ncurses again
timer.c, asciianm.c :
             - Ctrl-C and the change of the size of the window do not come in the
               middle of the drawing of a frame
Makefile :
             - New, without -m486. With ncurses if it is there, else ANSI only.
               Makefile.CURSES, Makefile.ANSI and INSTALL are not here
